{
  "esm": "2.1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "sectional_lr2m_high_triangle",
    "description": "True when the mean volume of section j sits in the UPPER third of the section, x >= 2/3 with x = sectional_lr2m_position: the reconstruction is cut back to a triangle on [vb[j+1] - 3 (vb[j+1] - vbar), vb[j+1]] that vanishes at its bottom (sectional_lr2m_support_bottom). Exclusive of sectional_lr2m_low_triangle (x <= 1/3), so the two cut-backs never compete. MOSAIC's form, vbar/vb[j] >= 0.9999 + 2 gamma/3, carries an absolute ratio margin that does not shrink with the section width; see sectional_lr2m_low_triangle for why the position form is used and why it reproduces MOSAIC wherever MOSAIC's margins do not overlap.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:stencil",
      "family:finite_volume",
      "grid:sectional_volume_1d",
      "op:advection",
      "order:2",
      "scheme:linear-discrete"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Zaveri, R. A., Easter, R. C., Fast, J. D., & Peters, L. K. (2008). Model for Simulating Aerosol Interactions and Chemistry (MOSAIC). Journal of Geophysical Research, 113, D13204.",
        "doi": "10.1029/2007JD008782"
      },
      {
        "citation": "WRF-Chem v4.8.0 chem/module_mosaic_movesect.F, subroutines move_sections_calc_masnumadvect and move_sections_apply_moves (R. C. Easter), the 'linear-discrete' / mass-number-advection section-moving algorithm (msectional = 20)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [
    {
      "ref": "./sectional_lr2m_position.esm"
    },
    {
      "ref": "../grid.esm"
    }
  ],
  "expression_templates": {
    "sectional_lr2m_high_triangle": {
      "params": ["N", "V", "c", "j"],
      "body": {
        "op": ">=",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "sectional_lr2m_position",
            "bindings": {"N": "N", "V": "V", "c": "c", "j": "j"}
          },
          {"op": "/", "args": [2, 3]}
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
